  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;be respectively the absolute maximum and the absolute minimum values of the function, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math> in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo></math> . Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
